# This repository manages line endings BY HAND. A handful of files are CRLF
# (transfer.md, docs/results/*.md, models/README.md, scripts/eval/README.md,
# .gitignore) and everything else is LF — see transfer.md §7 and CLAUDE.md.
#
# `* -text` disables ALL of git's automatic end-of-line conversion, so a clone on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true (the Git-for-Windows default) cannot silently
# flip every LF file to CRLF on checkout and then commit the flip back. Attributes
# win over config, so this protects the repo regardless of the friend's git setup.
* -text

# Binary blobs: no EOL handling, and no attempt to text-diff them.
*.pt     binary
*.pth    binary
*.onnx   binary
*.pkl    binary
*.tflite binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.tar    binary
*.parquet binary
*.npy    binary
*.npz    binary
